===Etymology===
Related to how quiet the shoes are.  {{suffix|en|sneak|er}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsnikɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-sneaker.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːkə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[sneak]]s.
#* {{RQ:Lamb Essays of Elia|passage=Beshrew the man who on such a day as this, the ''general festival'', should affect to stand aloof. I am none of those sneakers. I am free of the corporation, and care not who knows it.}}
# {{lb|en|US|Atlantic Canada|Australia|New Zealand}} An [[athletic]] [[shoe]] with a soft, [[rubber]] [[sole]]. A {{m|en|trainer|id=sneaker}}.
# {{lb|en|UK|dialect|archaic}} A [[vessel]] of [[drink]].
#* ''Spectator''
#*: I have just left the right worshipful and his myrmidons about a '''sneaker''' of five gallons!
# {{lb|en|India|archaic}} A large [[cup]] (or small [[basin]]) with a [[saucer]] and [[cover]].
# {{lb|en|biology}} A [[sneaker male]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Faye Flam|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=q2ZfAscW27oC&pg=PT86&dq=%22a+sneaker%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjbvsjntsnQAhVO7GMKHQYsBX84ChDoAQg2MAU#v=onepage&q=%22a%20sneaker%22&f=false|title=The Score: The Science of the Male Sex Drive|passage=These '''sneakers''' may go on this way indefinitely, or, if one of the big males somehow dies or disappears, a sneaker male's hormones will trigger a huge growth spurt and he'll metamorphose into an alpha male.}}

